mb","ingredient/lamb"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Dill","ingredient/dill"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"],["Beans","ingredient/beans"],["Legumes","ingredient/legumes"],["Vegetables","ingredient/vegetables"],["Brassica oleracea","ingredient/brassica-oleracea"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Mentha","ingredient/mentha"],["Qatiq","ingredient/qatiq"],["Spinach","ingredient/spinach"],["Yogurt","ingredient/yogurt"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/7/7a/Mercado_de_Chorsu_02.jpg/500px-Mercado_de_Chorsu_02.jpg","w":500,"h":314,"by":"LBM1948","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mercado_de_Chorsu_02.jpg"}},"ingredient/bumbu-seasoning":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/bumbu-seasoning","n":"Bumbu (seasoning)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Bumbu is the Indonesian word for a blend of spices and for pastes and it commonly appears in the names of spice mixtures, sauces and seasoning pastes. The official Indonesian language dictionary describes bumbu as \"various types of herbs and plants that have a pleasant aroma and flavour — such as ginger, turmeric, galangal, nutmeg and pepper — used to enhance the flavour of the food.\""]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bumbu-seasoning"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumbu_(seasoning)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Gulai","dish/gulai"]]],["Padang food","cuisine/padang-food",[["Gulai","dish/gulai"]]],["Singaporean Chinese cuisine","cuisine/singaporean-cuisine-chinese-inspired",[["Gulai","dish/gulai"]]],["S